      "writtenOn": "2023-09-08T01:56:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If my understanding is right, memcpy_repmovs comes from this [line](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/gpu/graphite/UploadTask.cpp;l\u003d162).\n```\n        } else {\n            writer.write(mipOffset, src, srcRowBytes, dstRowBytes, trimRowBytes, currentHeight);\n        }\n\n```\n\nMy current solution is to simply split buffer assignment and actual buffer write, so that the costly ops like buffer map and copy only happen as necessarily as needed.",
